# Clinical documents and external datasets are NOT committed.
#
# UNTH-DATA-GOVERNANCE.md forbids putting identifiable patient documents in this
# repository, and forbids redistributing external datasets whose licences do not
# permit it. A rule people have to remember is not a control; this file is the
# control. Anyone with repository access can read anything committed here, and a
# document committed once stays in the history after it is deleted.
#
# If you find yourself wanting to force-add an image, the answer is no. Ask.

# Every image, anywhere under this tree.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.webp
*.tif
*.tiff
*.pdf
*.heic

# Ground-truth transcriptions contain the clinical text of the documents, which
# can identify a case even when the image does not.
unth/ground-truth/*
!unth/ground-truth/.gitkeep
!unth/ground-truth/EXAMPLE.txt

# External datasets: large, and several may not be redistributed.
external/*/*
!external/*/.gitkeep
!external/**/PROVENANCE.md

# Reports may quote transcribed clinical text verbatim in error tables.
reports/**
!reports/.gitkeep

# The manifest and metadata are safe to commit ONLY because they carry no
# patient identifiers and no writer names — see UNTH-DATA-GOVERNANCE.md §3.
!unth/manifests/*.csv
!unth/metadata/*.json
